[swarren@convex.com (Steve Warren) writes:]
{{{... in response to move pet feature ...}}}
[] I think that the obvious solution is kicking.  Kicking your pet should not
[] beinterpreted by the game as an attack against your pet, but rather an
[] attempt to motivate it to get out of your way.  Thus it should not do any
[] hit-point damage to your pet and it should not cause you to loose any luck
[] or anger dieties.

i agree with this sentiment but have one reservation: suppose i do want
to kick my pet?  i think a movepet option (default on) would be best.
although it should probably replace safepet, it could possibly work in
conjunction with confirm and safepet:

if (safepet) then
  if (movepet) then simply_swap
  else stop_before_hitting
else
  if (confirm) then ask_before_hitting
  else attack

